 "text": "Hey there, how are you feeling? Drawing is truly about thinking rather than talent. Pick a simple subject, keep lines thin with light hands, and don't judge at the end of a few minutes. Find a picture you like and copy it carefully. Start on a fresh page in your sketchbook so you build confidence. Drawing with a pencil or dead using a sharp pen. A pencil leaves marks you can see, a pen is like a pencil but quieter. Nice of you to help now. Start with simple lines, and draw from life instead of pictures.",
